doc.para:
In-Expression Dictionary Arrays By using %[ ], you can write an object of the Dictionary class inline within an expression. List expressions for initial elements, separating element name => element value with commas. For example, if you write:
var dic = %["a" => 1, "b" => 2, "c" => 3];
a reference to a Dictionary class object whose element name and value pairs are "a":1, "b":2, and "c":3 will be assigned to dic. Internally, => is exactly the same as a comma, but => is allowed for readability (same as in Perl).
